training segment census includes the forward loss: true
training segment census includes every parameter gradient and optimizer write: true
every tiny training segment executes with a positive standalone time: true
a host-gated census before execution includes its separately compiled optimizer: true
that pre-execution census includes every optimizer parameter write: true
the emitted result line parses as one JSON object: true
framework is ocannl: true
backend names the backend the cell ran on: true
workload names the self-test model, not a benchmark cell: true
variant names the self-test: true
precision is f32: true
compile_s is a non-negative number: true
searched is false in an untuned cell: true
step_ms carries all three percentiles: true
every reported percentile is a positive time: true
the percentiles are emitted in order p10 <= p50 <= p90: true
queued_step_ms is a positive time: true
peak_memory_bytes is a positive byte count on every backend: true
and it names the counter it was read from, in both spellings: true
dominant_kernel names a kernel timed on its own, with a positive time: true
its verdict is one the report renders, and a number is printed exactly when exact: true
timed_steps is the count the protocol asked for: true
losses carries one parity checksum per parity step: true
every parity checksum is a finite number: true
